'Example 04 - Simply supported steel beam, cross-section optimization
'All design variables and all objectives are gh_/ghc_ prefixed, so both
'Search Variables and Search Results can auto-detect them with Filter
'Names left empty. Intended to be wired directly into Galapagos or
'Wallacei as: genome = gh_b, gh_h / fitness = minimize ghc_area subject
'to ghc_util_bending <= 1 and ghc_util_defl <= 1.

q = 25N/mm'uniform load on the beam (=25 kN/m)
L = 6000mm'span
fy = 235MPa'steel yield strength (S235)
E = 210000MPa'steel modulus of elasticity

gh_b = 150mm'DESIGN VARIABLE: beam width (genome)
gh_h = 300mm'DESIGN VARIABLE: beam height (genome)

M = q*L^2/8'maximum bending moment
W = gh_b*gh_h^2/6'elastic section modulus
I = gh_b*gh_h^3/12'second moment of area
sigma = M/W'bending stress
delta = 5*q*L^4/(384*E*I)'maximum midspan deflection
delta_allow = L/300'serviceability deflection limit

ghc_area = gh_b*gh_h'OBJECTIVE: cross-sectional area - minimize (proxy for material use)
ghc_util_bending = sigma/fy'CONSTRAINT: bending utilization - keep <= 1
ghc_util_defl = delta/delta_allow'CONSTRAINT: deflection utilization - keep <= 1
